cause: MAINTENANCE
effect: DETOUR
header_text {
  translation {
    text: "Shuttle buses replacing A Line, B Line, G Line and N Line beginning at 2:52 PM due to maintenance."
    language: "en"
  }
}
description_text {
  translation {
    text: "RTD will conduct federally required maintenance work that will affect commuter rail service on A, B, G, and N lines traveling to and from Union Station Saturday, Jan. 31, and Sunday, Feb. 1.\r\n\nService on the commuter rail lines to and from Union Station will be interrupted over a 48-hour period beginning Saturday and continuing through the end of service on Sunday. Expanded shuttle service will connect customers between affected stations. Regular service for all lines will resume Monday, Feb. 2.\r\n\nA Line: RTD will provide bus shuttle service for A Line customers between Union Station and 38th-Blake Station.\r\n\n    A Line customers at Union Station can access the shuttle at Gate B22 in the underground bus concourse\r\n    A Line customers at 38th-Blake Station can access the shuttle at the bus bridge gate on Blake Street\r\n    A Line service will operate as normal between 38th-Blake Station and Denver Airport Station\r\n\nB and G Lines: RTD will provide bus shuttle service for B and G Line customers between Union Station and 41st-Fox Station.\r\n\n    B and G Line customers at Union Station can access the shuttle at Gate B22 in the underground bus concourse\r\n    B and G Line customers at 41st-Fox Station can access the shuttle at Gate D\r\n    B Line service will operate as normal between 41st-Fox Station and Westminster Station\r\n    G Line service will operate as normal between 41st-Fox Station and Wheat Ridge-Ward Road Station\r\n\nN Line: RTD will provide bus shuttle service for N Line customers between Union Station and 48th & Brighton-National Western Center Station.\r\n\n    N Line customers at Union Station can access the shuttle at Gate B22 in the underground bus concourse\r\n    At 48th& Brighton-National Western Center Station, customers can access shuttle service at the bus stop at the station\r\n    N Line service will operate as normal between 48th& Brighton-National Western Center Station and Eastlake-124th Station\r\n\nCustomers should anticipate delays due to the rail closure and are encouraged to explore alternate routes on the RTD website if their trips are affected.\r\nAffected stops:\r\nUnion Station"
    language: "en"
  }
}
